.Bd -literal
=head1 DESCRIPTION
.Ed
.Fn X509_get0_signature
sets
.Nm *psig
to the signature of
.Ar x
and
.Ar *palg
to the signature algorithm of
.Ar x .
The values returned are internal pointers which
.Ar MUST NOT
be freed up after the call.
.Pp
.Xr X509_set0_signature 3
and
.Fn X509_REQ_set1_signature_algo
are the equivalent setters for the two values of
.Fn X509_get0_signature .
.Pp
.Fn X509_get0_tbs_sigalg
returns the signature algorithm in the signed portion of
.Ar x .
.Pp
.Fn X509_get_signature_nid
returns the NID corresponding to the signature algorithm of
.Ar x .
.Pp
.Fn X509_REQ_get0_signature ,
.Fn X509_REQ_get_signature_nid
.Fn X509_CRL_get0_signature
and
.Fn X509_CRL_get_signature_nid
perform the same function for certificate requests and CRLs.
.Pp
.Fn X509_ACERT_get0_signature ,
.Fn X509_ACERT_get_signature_nid
and
.Fn X509_ACERT_get0_info_sigalg
perform the same function for attribute certificates.
.Pp
.Fn X509_get_signature_info
retrieves information about the signature of certificate
.Ar x .
The NID of the signing digest is written to
.Ar *mdnid ,
the public key algorithm to
.Ar *pknid ,
the effective security bits to
.Ar *secbits
and flag details to
.Ar *flags .
Any of the parameters can be set to
.Ar NULL
if the information is not required.
.Pp
.Fn X509_SIG_INFO_get
and
.Fn X509_SIG_INFO_set
get and set information about a signature in an
.Ar X509_SIG_INFO
structure.
They are only used by implementations of algorithms which need to set
custom signature information: most applications will never need to call
them.
.Sh NOTES
These functions provide lower level access to signatures in certificates
where an application wishes to analyse or generate a signature in a form
where
.Xr X509_sign 3
et al is not appropriate (for example a non standard or unsupported
format).
.Pp
The security bits returned by
.Fn X509_get_signature_info
refers to information available from the certificate signature (such as
the signing digest).
In some cases the actual security of the signature is less because the
signing key is less secure: for example a certificate signed using
SHA-512 and a 1024 bit RSA key.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn X509_get_signature_nid ,
.Fn X509_REQ_get_signature_nid
and
.Fn X509_CRL_get_signature_nid
return a NID.
.Pp
.Fn X509_get0_signature ,
.Fn X509_REQ_get0_signature
and
.Fn X509_CRL_get0_signature
do not return values.
.Pp
.Fn X509_get_signature_info
returns 1 if the signature information returned is valid or 0 if the
information is not available (e.g.
unknown algorithms or malformed parameters).
.Pp
.Fn X509_REQ_set1_signature_algo
returns 0 on success; or 1 on an error (e.g.
null ALGO pointer).
X509_REQ_set0_signature does not return an error value.
